From 066ad55c3b8330550d66a68d371e8476cf106c74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:42:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 021/144] wifi: ath12k: retain WCN7860 TME DMA memory through
 teardown

Keep only the TME-Lite protocol addition from the imported sequence. Reuse the existing M3, AUX and scoped QDSS paths and retain normal regdb/calibration handling. Bound firmware size before allocation; keep a dedicated coherent allocation across QMI responses and restarts, freeing it only after powerdown and event cancellation during deinit. Match the dedicated WCN7860 hardware revision and keep TME failure nonfatal as in the OEM caller.

Link: https://github.com/mrlund/linux-omarchy-mobile/commit/c098c11d610ec2b6d4bf94859435aa8c3064112f

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750/blob/d50b305f7da9e14715a25120a4ac7b1a4b8b97c3/vendor/qcom/opensource/wlan/platform/cnss2/main.c
(cherry picked from commit 2a68a50bdb67f59bdcd711904f8f32f55face124)

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0034-wifi-ath12k-retain-WCN7860-TME-DMA-memory-through-te.patch
Import-SHA256: 5d774c33a6db7f255c8c3dbff33c5dd795fdef08acc1ac25814ae6e5cb5a9e09
